{"action_id":null,"arguments":[],"assumptions":[{"assumption_id":"node.dfbeb05a271dfdc22f59b8d9.a0","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"Footnote 5's unqualified direction to confirm and demonstrate has independent operative effect for its stated minimum content.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.dfbeb05a271dfdc22f59b8d9.a1","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"This reading retains paragraph 14's request condition for any broader demonstration and recognizes the resulting textual tension.","status":"PROVISIONAL"}],"bundle_hash":"9423aadbc474331e78a4d722744157a087df709070db72beb233b95af356f085","candidate_id":"candidate.44f4d4f7c3d5425fb307670ad8566353","controlled_language":"[TRUE_IS_SATISFIED] Within the Product Provider scope, true means the condition for the minimum demonstration specified by footnote 5 is satisfied independently of an SFC request. The constant true expresses this proposed unconditional activation, not an invented fact or a finding that demonstration occurred; false does not arise within scope on this reading. Footnote 5 can be read as independently requiring both confirmation and demonstration to the SFC of compliance with paragraphs 10–13 and the high-confidence smart-contract proposition. With no request, that minimum demonstration would remain expected, while paragraph 14 still expressly conditions its broader demonstration on a request. The precise confidence and satisfaction standards remain unresolved. Paragraphs 15 and 16 still require their respective requests for third-party audit or verification and a satisfactory supporting legal opinion; footnote 5 does not expressly expand those provisions.","disposition_reason":"Unreviewed interpretation proposal","family_ids":["dependencies"],"generation_phase":"BLIND_INITIAL","issue_ids":[],"parent_id":null,"probability_of_legal_correctness":null,"revision_reason":"Unlike the request-conditioned reading, the omission of a request qualification in footnote 5 creates an independently expected minimum demonstration. This is textually possible but weaker because it reduces the work done by paragraph 14's express condition. It supplies no basis for removing the separate request conditions in paragraphs 15 and 16.","run_id":"run.8adc12b432874c5bb1e8b4730a0ab93f","scheduling_priority":0,"schema_version":"interpretation.v1","score_purpose":"INVESTIGATION_PRIORITY_ONLY","source_packet_hash":"d74180e126dda06342060a17b37c3227fc695e9fc0f0d5ce68b187d7cb8bc612","source_unit_ids":["dc689bdf0ffcf.u3.944","dc689bdf0ffcf.u4.1185","dc689bdf0ffcf.u5.1464","dc689bdf0ffcf.u6.1694"],"status":"ACTIVE","subject_unit":"Footnote 5 as an independent minimum demonstration requirement"}